<title>USA: ESC Medical Q1 operating profit rises.</title>
<headline>ESC Medical Q1 operating profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company based ni YOKNEAM, Israel</p>
<p>				ESC MEDICAL SYSTEMS LTD.</p>
<p>		 Condensed Consolidated Statement of Operations</p>
<p>				     (in thousands)</p>
<p>							Three months ended</p>
<p>					 Mar 31, 1997	Mar 31, 1996</p>
<p>				    (Unaudited)  (Unaudited Restated)</p>
<p> Sales					 22,961		10,100</p>
<p> Cost of Sales				6,471		 2,927</p>
<p> Gross Profit				16,490		 7,173</p>
<p> Research and Development Costs, net  2,726		   934</p>
<p> Selling &amp; Marketing Expenses	   6,715		 3,093</p>
<p> General &amp; Administrative		 1,451		   897</p>
<p> Total Operating Expenses		10,892		 4,924</p>
<p> Operating Income			   5,598		 2,249</p>
<p> Financing income, net			498		   299</p>
<p>						  6,096		 2,548</p>
<p> Expenses in connection with merger			   4,650</p>
<p> Income before income tax		 1,446		 2,548</p>
<p> Income taxes				   440		   162</p>
<p> Net income				   1,006		 2,386</p>
<p> EPS					     0.05		  0.13</p>
<p> Weighted average number of shares   20,459		18,253</p>
<p>EPS excluding the expenses connected</p>
<p> with the merger of Luxar Corp.	  0.28		  0.13</p>
<p>*  MERGER OF LUXAR CORPORATION (&quot;LUXAR&quot;)</p>
<p>	     In the quarter ended March 31, 1997, Luxar was</p>
<p>merged with and into ESC through the issuance of up to 2,500,000 Ordinary shares and options of ESC.  The merger with Luxar was accounted for as a pooling of interests, and accordingly, all prior period financial statements have been restated to include the accounts of Luxar and reflect the issuance of the shares and options of ESC.</p>
<p>	     The statement of operations for the quarter ended</p>
<p>March 31, 1997, reflects nonrecurring expenses of approximately $4.6 million related to costs associated with the merger.</p>
<p>	 Prior to the merger, Luxar used a fiscal year ending</p>
<p>September 30.</p>
<p>	 The restated profit and loss statements combine the</p>
<p>first quarter ended December 31, 1995 of Luxar with the first quarter ended March 31, 1996 of ESC.  The net income for the three month period ended December 31, 1996 for Luxar was reflected as an adjustment to retained earnings under shareholders' equity effective January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
